on walls but also corporation  around the education  and um all the uh engagements beyond  um the university itself with business  and policy makers  uh okay what would you say are the top  three  most important scientific advancements  we have to get done  in order to to achieve your goals  so there are many different areas where  there's actually currently today  exciting science on being undertaken to  help drive  drivers towards a zero carbon future but  if i was to pick three areas  the first would be in the area of energy  technologies particularly  battery storage technologies we know  that so much of our world is going to be  transitioned to an electric world  and having that battery storage is  critically important to underpin that  the second area that i would point to is  transport it's another major part of our  emissions  we know that our ground transport our  cars are  very rapidly moving towards  electrification  but aviation is a is a key part of our  transport system  and looking to see how we can deliver  zero carbon aviation  into the future is a is a is a critical  research challenge  at the moment and then the final area  that i would point to is greenhouse gas  removal  um if we are to address climate change  we're going to need to find  ways of actively removing greenhouse  gases from the atmosphere either by  technological means  or by natural means enhancing nature in  a way that can  help the climate problem but if we're  going to do that we need to ensure that  at the same time  it's also helping the biodiversity  crisis that we're also experiencing at  the moment  well we're looking forward to meet you  again during the  session at the summit here thank you so  much for sharing your insights emily  schachberg thanks a lot for this talk  thank you
 

